      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and many clinicians cap it at 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max IR dose.\n- **500 mg three times daily**, or **1000 mg twice daily**.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, perhaps split into two or three doses.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that too, and include the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note. I'll enter it once you confirm."
      }
     ],
